#import "template.typ": policy-rule, policy-warning

= Approval Workflows & Delegation of Authority

== Managerial Approval Hierarchy

All expense claims must be reviewed and digitally signed off by an authorized manager before disbursement by Finance.

#policy-rule("POL-APP-001", "Approval Authority Limits")[
  Approval authority is tiered based on the total claim value:
  - *Tier 1 (Up to €1,000 / \$1,000)*: Direct Line Manager
  - *Tier 2 (€1,001 to €5,000 / \$1,001 to \$5,000)*: Department Director / Head of Function
  - *Tier 3 (Over €5,000 / \$5,000)*: Vice President and Head of Finance
]

== Pre-Approval Requirements

Certain high-cost expenditures require written approval before commitments are made.

#policy-rule("POL-APP-002", "Mandatory Travel Pre-Approval")[
  All international travel, intercontinental flights, group offsite bookings, and expenditures expected to exceed €2,500 / \$2,500 require written pre-approval from the relevant Department Director prior to booking or incurring the expense.
]

== Prohibition of Self-Approval

Integrity of controls prohibits self-authorization of corporate expenditures.

#policy-warning("POL-APP-003", "No Self-Approval")[
  No employee may approve their own expense report, regardless of seniority or corporate title. Claims submitted by the Chief Executive Officer must be approved by the Chair of the Audit Committee.
]
